---
import { Code } from 'astro:components'
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro'
import Sloth from '../components/Sloth.astro'

const snippet = `import { slauth } from 'slauth'
import { d1 } from 'slauth/stores/d1'
import { resend } from 'slauth/email/resend'

const auth = slauth({
  secret: env.SLAUTH_SECRET,
  store: d1(env.DB),
  email: resend({ apiKey: env.RESEND_KEY, from: 'hi@myapp.dev' }),
})

// Every sign-in route, mounted in one line:
if (url.pathname.startsWith('/auth/')) return auth.handle(request)

// And in your own routes:
const user = await auth.user(request) // { id, email } or null`

const html = `<script type="module">import 'slauth/element'</script>

<slauth-sign-in app-name="My App" redirect="/"></slauth-sign-in>`

const features = [
  { icon: '📬', title: 'Email codes', body: 'Six digits in their inbox, ten minutes to use them. No passwords to store, reset or leak.' },
  { icon: '🔑', title: 'Passkeys', body: 'Face ID, Touch ID or a security key. Real WebAuthn, checked with Web Crypto, no libraries.' },
  { icon: '🗄️', title: 'Your database', body: 'D1, SQLite, Workers KV, memory, or any get/put/delete. Your users never live on someone else’s server.' },
  { icon: '📌', title: 'PIN app lock', body: 'An optional 4-digit PIN on top, asked every visit, daily, weekly or never. Each person chooses.' },
  { icon: '🌍', title: 'Runs anywhere', body: 'Cloudflare Workers, Bun, Deno, Node, Next.js, Astro, Hono. If it speaks Request/Response, it works.' },
  { icon: '🪶', title: 'Zero dependencies', body: 'About 29 kB of plain JavaScript with types. Read the whole thing over a coffee.' },
]
---
<Site title="slauth: auth for side projects" description="Email codes and passkeys in five minutes. Your database, zero dependencies, runs anywhere. Less fuss than Clerk, sturdier than a hard-coded password.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="stickers">
          <span class="sticker">v1 · MIT</span>
          <span class="sticker leaf">zero dependencies</span>
          <span class="sticker pink">no invoices</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Auth for <span class="highlight">side projects</span>.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Slow sloth, fast login. Email codes and passkeys in five minutes, in <em>your</em> database, on whatever you deploy to. Sturdier than a password in an env var, and a lot less fuss than a hosted auth company.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Get started →</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/silicondaydream/slauth">Star on GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <button class="copy-pill" type="button" data-copy="npm install slauth"><span class="prompt">$</span> npm install slauth <span aria-hidden="true">📋</span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-demo">
        <Sloth hang size="100%" class="hero-sloth" title="A sloth hanging from a branch" />
        <div class="demo-wrap">
          <slauth-sign-in app-name="the demo" base-path="/demo-auth" no-passkeys></slauth-sign-in>
          <div class="inbox card" id="inbox" hidden>
            <strong>📬 Demo inbox</strong>
            <p>Your code is <code id="inbox-code"></code>. (On a real app, it's an email.)</p>
          </div>
          <div class="inbox card" id="welcome" hidden>
            <strong>🎉 Signed in!</strong>
            <p>That's the whole flow. <a href="#" id="again">Try again</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block tint">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>This is the whole server.</h2>
        <p class="muted">One function, one store, one line to mount the routes. Then ask <code>auth.user(request)</code> who's there. No dashboard to configure, no SDK to keep in sync, no webhook to babysit.</p>
        <p class="aside-note">The sloth wrote this part very slowly so you don't have to.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="code-stack">
        <div class="code-card">
          <div class="bar"><span class="dot" style="background:#f7b2c6"></span><span class="dot" style="background:#f59e0b"></span><span class="dot" style="background:#7aa340"></span>&nbsp;worker.js</div>
          <Code code={snippet} lang="js" theme="vitesse-dark" />
        </div>
        <div class="code-card">
          <div class="bar"><span class="dot" style="background:#f7b2c6"></span><span class="dot" style="background:#f59e0b"></span><span class="dot" style="background:#7aa340"></span>&nbsp;index.html</div>
          <Code code={html} lang="html" theme="vitesse-dark" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Everything a side project needs.<br /><span class="muted">Nothing it doesn't.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid three">
        {features.map((f) => (
          <article class="card feature">
            <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true">{f.icon}</div>
            <h3>{f.title}</h3>
            <p class="muted">{f.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p class="muted">Three steps, and the middle one is your users checking their email.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="card"><span class="num">1</span><h3>They type their email</h3><p class="muted">slauth emails a 6-digit code (or prints it in your terminal while you build).</p></li>
        <li class="card"><span class="num">2</span><h3>They type the code</h3><p class="muted">A session cookie is set. It's HttpOnly, the token is stored hashed, and it lasts 30 days from the last visit.</p></li>
        <li class="card"><span class="num">3</span><h3>Next time: a passkey</h3><p class="muted">One tap to add a passkey, and signing in is just their face or fingerprint from then on.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap grid two">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>👍 Great for</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Side projects, prototypes and hackathon apps</li>
          <li>Tools for you, your family and friends</li>
          <li>Small apps that should own their users' data</li>
          <li>A suite of apps that share one sign-in</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🙅 Not for (use something bigger)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Enterprise SSO, SAML or SCIM</li>
          <li>Teams, orgs and role management</li>
          <li>Compliance paperwork (SOC 2 and friends)</li>
          <li>"Sign in with 40 different providers"</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="aside-note">We'd rather tell you now than after you've built on it. <a href="/compare">See how it compares →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block cta">
    <div class="wrap cta-inner card">
      <Sloth mood="sleepy" size={150} />
      <div>
        <h2>Go build the fun part.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Sign-in is done. Five minutes, no credit card, no "talk to sales".</p>
        <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Read the quickstart →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>

<script>
  import '../../../src/element.js'

  // The demo talks to a pretend server that lives in this page, so you can try the
  // real <slauth-sign-in> without an inbox. A real app talks to auth.handle().
  const realFetch = window.fetch.bind(window)
  let pending = ''
  const inbox = document.getElementById('inbox')!
  const welcome = document.getElementById('welcome')!
  const reply = (status: number, body: object) => new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status, headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' } })

  window.fetch = async (input: RequestInfo | URL, init?: RequestInit) => {
    const url = typeof input === 'string' ? input : input instanceof URL ? input.href : input.url
    if (!url.startsWith('/demo-auth/')) return realFetch(input, init)
    const body = init?.body ? JSON.parse(String(init.body)) : {}
    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 350))
    if (url.endsWith('email/start')) {
      if (!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(body.email ?? '')) return reply(400, { error: "That doesn't look like an email address.", code: 'bad-email' })
      pending = String(Math.floor(100000 + Math.random() * 900000))
      document.getElementById('inbox-code')!.textContent = pending
      inbox.hidden = false
      return reply(200, { ok: true })
    }
    if (url.endsWith('email/verify')) {
      if (String(body.code).trim() !== pending) return reply(400, { error: 'That code is wrong.', code: 'bad-code' })
      return reply(200, { user: { id: 'usr_demo', email: body.email, createdAt: Date.now() } })
    }
    return reply(404, { error: 'Not found.', code: 'not-found' })
  }

  const box = document.querySelector('slauth-sign-in')!
  box.addEventListener('slauth:signed-in', () => {
    inbox.hidden = true
    welcome.hidden = false
    ;(box as HTMLElement).hidden = true
  })
  document.getElementById('again')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault()
    welcome.hidden = true
    ;(box as HTMLElement).hidden = false
  })

  for (const pill of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]')) {
    pill.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(pill.dataset.copy!)
        const was = pill.lastElementChild!.textContent
        pill.lastElementChild!.textContent = '✅'
        setTimeout(() => (pill.lastElementChild!.textContent = was), 1200)
      } catch {}
    })
  }
</script>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 48px 0 64px; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; gap: 40px; align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; } .hero { padding: 72px 0 88px; } }
  .stickers { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .stickers .sticker:nth-child(2) { transform: rotate(1.5deg); }
  .lede { font-size: 19px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 560px; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .hero-demo { position: relative; display: grid; justify-items: center; }
  .hero-sloth { width: min(260px, 70%); height: auto; margin-bottom: -38px; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .demo-wrap { width: 100%; max-width: 360px; position: relative; z-index: 2; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  slauth-sign-in { --slauth-font: var(--font); --slauth-ink: #2b2118; }
  .inbox { padding: 14px 16px; font-size: 15px; transform: rotate(1deg); background: #fff8d6; color: #2b2118; }
  .inbox p { margin: 4px 0 0; }
  .inbox code { font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 2px; }
  .two-col { display: grid; gap: 32px; }
  @media (min-width: 960px) { .two-col { grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; align-items: start; } }
  .code-stack { display: grid; gap: 18px; min-width: 0; }
  .code-card :global(pre) { margin: 0; padding: 18px; font-size: 13.5px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .feature .icon { font-size: 30px; width: 54px; height: 54px; display: grid; place-items: center; border: var(--line); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--bg-2); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .feature p { margin: 0; }
  .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 820px) { .steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .steps .num { display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 40px; height: 40px; border: var(--line); border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .steps p { margin: 0; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .cta-inner { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 24px; background: var(--accent); color: #2b2118; }
  .cta-inner .muted { color: #4a3a2b; }
  .cta-inner .btn.primary { background: #fff; color: #2b2118; }
</style>
